<title>UK: British jobless falls 35,600 in September.</title>
<headline>British jobless falls 35,600 in September.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's jobless total fell 35,600 to 2.07 million in September or 7.4 percent of the working population, official figures showed.</p>
<p>The jobless rate was 7.5 percent in August. The fall was greater than analysts had forecast and government bonds fell as the chances of an interest rate cut receded.</p>
</text>
